WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO Features/Admin errors; the sole blocker pre-exists this
              additive change and is unrelated to backup)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The full-app iOS build fails on EXACTLY ONE compile error, in an unrelated shared-surface file
  this commit neither introduces nor touches:

    TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions.swift:141:22:
      error: escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'
        private func glass(@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View) -> some View { TSGlassPanel { content() ... } }

  Provenance (proven pre-existing):
    - `git show HEAD:.../AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions.swift` contains the buggy `glass(...)`
      verbatim — added by commit 40e1e5da0 ("add AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions surface (P4)").
    - `git diff --stat HEAD -- apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/` -> empty (untouched by me).
    - The file references ZERO backup types (`grep -c Backup` -> 0); unrelated to this page.
    - grep "error:" iOS build log | grep -c "Features/Admin"  -> 0   (my code contributes no errors)

  An earlier build iteration surfaced 30 errors from a genuine NAME COLLISION my first draft
  introduced (a top-level `BackupRun`/`BackupRunStatus`/`BackupStatusChip` clashing with the
  existing dashboard-widget `BackupMonitorWidget`). That was MY regression and is FIXED: those
  types are namespaced to `BackupRestoreRun`/`BackupRestoreRunStatus`/`BackupRestoreStatusChip`
  (module-scope collision scan now clean). Post-fix the full-app build error count dropped 30 -> 1,
  the remaining 1 being the unrelated pre-existing AIGeofence bug above.

  macOS app target (TeslaSync-macOS) shares the same Sources, so it hits the same pre-existing
  AIGeofence error, plus development-signing (DEVELOPMENT_TEAM="" on this runner; ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME
  + entitlements) — the documented P4/P99 signed-acceptance-gate concern (apps/macos-pending-verifications.md).

  `xcodebuild test` is blocked by the same pre-existing compile error (the app must build first);
  the page's own 16 tests pass in the isolated Swift-6 harness above. Fixing AIGeofence is out of
  scope (allowed-files = Features/Admin/** + nav + catalog + log; task rule: do not fix unrelated
